  "labels": {
    "anya": "Инспектор",
    "leva": "Вика",
    "guest": "Дмитрий"
  },
  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The fire inspector continues his strict check and rejects several fire extinguishers. The restaurant owner, Dmitry, arrives and demands to know the real reason behind this sudden and aggressive inspection. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ваш огнетушитель?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Он висел здесь в прошлый раз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы что, смеётесь надо мной?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этот не подходит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот нормальный огнетушитель.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где его пломба?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можно узнать одну вещь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему у вас такой интерес к ресторану?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы боремся с плохим руководством.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Был звонок моему начальнику.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из соседнего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Всё понятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну что, до завтра.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ваш огнетушитель?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where is your fire extinguisher?' Notice the word order: 'where' comes first, and 'fire extinguisher' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Он висел здесь в прошлый раз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It was hanging here last time.' Notice the word order: 'he' comes first, and 'time' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы что, смеётесь надо мной?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you laughing at me?' A compact expression built around 'you' and 'me'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этот не подходит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This one is not suitable.' You'll hear 'is coming up' all the time in the show, here connected with 'is coming up'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот нормальный огнетушитель.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is a normal fire extinguisher.' The key word here means 'decent', which Vika combines with 'fire extinguisher'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где его пломба?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where is its seal?' A compact expression built around 'where' and 'seal'. Then Dmitry replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good afternoon.' Dmitry puts 'good' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'day'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можно узнать одну вещь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'May I know one thing?' In Russian, 'may' leads into 'thing' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему у вас такой интерес к ресторану?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why do you have such an interest in the restaurant?' In Russian, 'why' leads into 'restaurant' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы боремся с плохим руководством.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We are fighting with bad management.' A compact expression built around 'we' and 'leadership'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Был звонок моему начальнику.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There was a call to my boss.' Listen for the word meaning 'was' right alongside 'call' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из соседнего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'From the neighboring restaurant.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'neighboring' straight to 'restaurant'. Dmitry answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Всё понятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything is clear.' Notice the word order: 'clear' comes first, and 'clear' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну что, до завтра.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well then, until tomorrow.' Listen for the word meaning 'what' right alongside 'tomorrow' in this line. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ваш огнетушитель?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Он висел здесь в прошлый раз.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы что, смеётесь надо мной?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этот не подходит.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот нормальный огнетушитель.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где его пломба?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можно узнать одну вещь?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему у вас такой интерес к ресторану?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы боремся с плохим руководством.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Был звонок моему начальнику.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из соседнего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
